{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll","id":1402763,"title":"A Devil's Bargain (Roll)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-14T01:44:43-07:00","id":1402763,"title":"A Devil's Bargain (Roll)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Corebook page 216</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Bargain: Bargaining is similar to the persuade action, but doesn\u2019t depend on your target\u2019s Intimacies. Instead, you must offer a bribe, gift, or favor that the character you\u2019re convincing believes is worth the difficulty or danger of the task you\u2019re asking him to perform. The Storyteller should take into account the Intimacies, wealth, and social status of the character in deciding what they will consider sufficient payment (a wealthy noble is not going to be moved to favor your cause in court by the gift of an apple, though a starving beggar might be).</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Bargain action is used against a PC, who decides if the character being offered the Bargain thinks the payment is worth the action they're being asked to perform?<br /> <br /> I think it's the character's player, as they are the one who invented the character and knows what makes their character tick.<br /> <br /> A strict RAW reading might suggest it's the ST. What does Exalted Forum think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T02:45:09-07:00","id":1402772,"title":"","content":"To comment on the original discussion in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1402262#post1402262\">Ask a Question</a> which spawned this thread:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I think there's a miscommunication going on. The main point of contention hasn't been so much who should decide if an offer is sufficient. Rather people have been disputing the idea you put forth that there should be no roll in Bargains (and your ensuing statement that never rolling on Bargain actions is, in fact, how the system was designed to work, which is what got you a retort from Eric).<br /> <br /> To answer your OP, when everyone at the table is playing fair and understands the difference between a decision they would make and one their character would make, then I think it's simplest and makes the most sense to let the player decide. It's only if you have a player that is either acting in bad faith or simply has a hard time roleplaying their characters' decisions, that the ST (and the rest of the table, for that matter) should override them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T03:43:00-07:00","id":1402776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402772#post1402772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To comment on the original discussion in <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1402262#post1402262&quot;]Ask</a> a Question[/URL] which spawned this thread:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I think there's a miscommunication going on. The main point of contention hasn't been so much who should decide if an offer is sufficient. Rather people have been disputing the idea you put forth that there should be no roll in Bargains (and your ensuing statement that never rolling on Bargain actions is, in fact, how the system was designed to work, which is what got you a retort from Eric).<br /> <br /> To answer your OP, when everyone at the table is playing fair and understands the difference between a decision they would make and one their character would make, then I think it's simplest and makes the most sense to let the player decide. It's only if you have a player that is either acting in bad faith or simply has a hard time roleplaying their characters' decisions, that the ST (and the rest of the table, for that matter) should override them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> But let's say everyone is playing in good faith (whenever I post gameplay advice, you can take it as read that I'm assuming people are playing in good faith).<br /> <br /> My character is addicted to opium. I have a Flaw &quot;addicted to opium&quot;. I have a Major Principle &quot;I like taking opium&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sally Salesman offers me a hit of opium if I let her past the door I am supposed to be guarding.<br /> <br /> If I am playing in good faith... wouldn't I just take the deal (and the 2 Bonus XP) and let her go past? Why would you make Sally roll for that? Sally could have 4 dice. She could have 13 dice with double 7s. I want the opium, she wants to pass, just make the trade.<br /> <br /> If there's an important, compelling character reason for me to not let Sally past, is it <i>unreasonable</i> for me to say &quot;I know I'm playing a drug addict, but I'm a functioning addict. It is so important to my character that they guard this door that they are not going to just let someone past -- this offer isn't good enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> I say the former example just makes sense. Don't bog down your game with pointless rolls.<br /> <br /> I say in the latter example, the player knows the character better than the ST and the other players at the table and is entitled to make that call. That doesn't mean Sally doesn't get to pass, it means Sally has to offer something more than a single hit of opium. And when she offers something of sufficient worth... we loop back round to the first scenario -- why would I not just accept the trade?<br /> <br /> Now... I can see a middle ground where the player accepts that the trade is something the character might agree to, albeit reluctantly, and asks the NPC to roll against their Resolve. But this is a really niche middle ground, and, assuming good faith on the part of the player, I absolutely defend the player's right to say &quot;I am uncomfortable with this deal, I don't think what is being offered is sufficient&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you are playing in good faith, and someone offers your character sufficient payment to do something then you should do it. That's literally the definition of &quot;sufficient&quot;. If the payment offered is insufficient it means that you don't think the payment is worth what you are being asked to do... so the Bargain auto-fails. Just like a Persuade action auto-fails if doesn't hit a sufficient Intimacy. If you don't think the payment is worth the action, then the payment isn't worth the action. Period.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Now if a player at the table is playing in bad faith, you can't fix that with a dice roll against their character's Resolve. And there's a larger issue that you need to fix with an OOC conversation.<br /> <br /> If you try to beat down a PC by throwing dice at their character that is not going to fix poor player behaviour. I literally can't think of anything more counter-productive than that. I know Exalted doesn't have a Storytelling Chapter but this class in DMing 101 is called &quot;How to Lose Friends and Alienate People&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T04:24:09-07:00","id":1402780,"title":"","content":"I dunno man, in my mind what you see as a niche middle ground is pretty wide. I can see lots of cases where a roll can just swing the decision without anyone being upset over it.<br /> <br /> Let's take your example of Sally the Salesman offering the character... Let's call him Oscar the Opium Addict some opium.<br /> <br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> Sally walks up to Oscar, who is a massive O-head, and Sally knows this. But the door is also supposed to be guarded, Oscar knows this, and he has a minor intimacy that might apply as to why he wants to do a good job guarding that door. Or the player decides this should be Oscars moment to step up.<br /> <br /> So Sally offers Oscar the opium and it could go either way. If you take a step back and look at the situation, it is kind of obvious why it shouldn't be binary. Maybe Oscar is having a good day, or a bad day, might have slept good or bad, which might decide how he's feeling today, which will VASTLY differ the importance he ascribes to getting that hit of opium right the fuck now.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's perfectly valid to then follow the rules for social influence and roll the bargain to see how well Sally frames her offer, because maybe she needs to offer it in a way that lets Oscar keep a bit of his pride? <br /> And maybe Oscar is having a particularly good or bad day, helping or hindering him in his decision. <br /> I feel this is very well dealt with by a dice roll.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I could widen that niche middle ground for you on other examples as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T06:09:42-07:00","id":1402793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402780#post1402780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno man, in my mind what you see as a niche middle ground is pretty wide. I can see lots of cases where a roll can just swing the decision without anyone being upset over it.<br /> <br /> Let's take your example of Sally the Salesman offering the character... Let's call him Oscar the Opium Addict some opium.<br /> <br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> Sally walks up to Oscar, who is a massive O-head, and Sally knows this. But the door is also supposed to be guarded, Oscar knows this, and he has a minor intimacy that might apply as to why he wants to do a good job guarding that door. Or the player decides this should be Oscars moment to step up.<br /> <br /> So Sally offers Oscar the opium and it could go either way. If you take a step back and look at the situation, it is kind of obvious why it shouldn't be binary. Maybe Oscar is having a good day, or a bad day, might have slept good or bad, which might decide how he's feeling today, which will VASTLY differ the importance he ascribes to getting that hit of opium right the fuck now.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's perfectly valid to then follow the rules for social influence and roll the bargain to see how well Sally frames her offer, because maybe she needs to offer it in a way that lets Oscar keep a bit of his pride? <br /> And maybe Oscar is having a particularly good or bad day, helping or hindering him in his decision. <br /> I feel this is very well dealt with by a dice roll.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I could widen that niche middle ground for you on other examples as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who decides if Oscar is in a good mood or a bad mood? Who decides if Oscar is going to step up?<br /> <br /> I contend that the player decides what their character does. The player decides if they're going to rescue the princess or guard the door or go get high.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about NPCs, then sure, make the roll.<br /> <br /> But Oscar isn't a character in a book. And he's not a real person. He's MY character. I make the decisions for my character.<br /> <br /> In combat, I decide whether I take an Aim action or an Attack action. You don't get to say &quot;Aiming is unrealistic, you have to Attack&quot;. I get to choose what my character does.<br /> <br /> If you insult my character, I decide whether I laugh it off or challenge you to a duel. That's the point of me playing.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;following the rules&quot; the rules say, in black and white, that the offer must be &quot;worth the difficulty or danger of the task you\u2019re asking him to perform&quot;. I am advocating that you follow the rules -- you must offer something which is worth it.<br /> <br /> The question is, who decides what's worth it?<br /> <br /> If the player decides that an offer is worth it, just accept the offer. If the player decides it isn't worth it, then <i>according to the rules</i>, the Bargain fails.<br /> <br /> If the ST decides that Oscar is having a bad day and the opium hit seems worth it to him, then sure that blows the middle ground a mile wide. But I contend that this shouldn't happen -- the player should decide whether Oscar is having a bad day.<br /> <br /> Oscar and Sally don't exist. John, the player, and Chesire, the ST, exist. Oscar doesn't get a say: John decides what is and isn't important to Oscar, and John decides if Oscar is going to step up or shirk off. Because Oscar isn't real. Oscar doesn't want to descend into the Labyrinth and foil the plots of the thousand year old Deathlords. Oscar doesn't <i>want</i> anything. Oscar exists purely as a vessel for me to tell a story. I invented Oscar. I made him a drug addict. I made him a functioning drug addict. I know exactly how strong his addiction is, because I'm the one who invented him. I know how much he cares about guarding a door, because I'm the one who decided he cares about guarding the door. I should be the one who decides if he cares more about guarding the door or getting high.<br /> <br /> For NPCs, this is a completely different equation. For NPCs, the ST has discretion and the middle ground is truly enormous.<br /> <br /> If Sally is a PC and Oscar is an NPC, then roll away.<br /> <br /> But there's a fundamental difference between NPCs and PCs.<br /> <br /> Are you honestly saying that I shouldn't be allowed to say &quot;My character, Oscar, doesn't think Sally's offer to let her pass for a hit of opium is worth the danger that puts him in&quot;? You're saying I don't get to make that decision for my character? Who does get to make it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T06:29:23-07:00","id":1402796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402776#post1402776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I am playing in good faith... wouldn't I just take the deal (and the 2 Bonus XP) and let her go past? Why would you make Sally roll for that? Sally could have 4 dice. She could have 13 dice with double 7s. I want the opium, she wants to pass, just make the trade.<br /> <br /> If there's an important, compelling character reason for me to not let Sally past, is it <i>unreasonable</i> for me to say &quot;I know I'm playing a drug addict, but I'm a functioning addict. It is so important to my character that they guard this door that they are not going to just let someone past -- this offer isn't good enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> I say the former example just makes sense. Don't bog down your game with pointless rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying your way of running bargains is unreasonable, just that it's a house rule rather than how the system is designed to work.<br /> <br /> To me the intent seems to be that a &quot;sufficient&quot; offer is one that can reasonably tempt your character. If your character is tempted by an offer and is fine with it, the trade goes through, no roll. But if they know beneath the temptation that they should turn it down, that's when the Bargain roll kicks in. Ideally the character's player decides if the character is in that situation or not.<br /> <br /> If your drug addict is actually meaningfully tempted by the drug on offer, then the offer is sufficient and a Bargain roll is gonna happen. If it's important to you that your character is a functioning addict, then now is the time to Excellency your Resolve and whatnot. Simply wanting the character to be a functioning addict isn't enough to resist the temptation if you haven't built the character to be able to. Much like you can't block attacks simply by saying &quot;my character is a deadly warrior, so this attack is insufficient to hit him&quot; (I know that example is a bit extreme, but you get the point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 07-14-2020, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T06:43:36-07:00","id":1402799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402796#post1402796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying your way of running bargains is unreasonable, just that it's a house rule rather than how the system is designed to work.<br /> <br /> To me the intent seems to be that a &quot;sufficient&quot; offer is one that can reasonably tempt your character. If your character is tempted by an offer and is fine with it, the trade goes through, no roll. But if they know beneath the temptation that they should turn it down, that's when the Bargain roll kicks in. As I said before, ideally the character's player decides if the character is in that situation or not.<br /> <br /> If your drug addict is actually meaningfully tempted by the drug on offer, then the offer is sufficient and a Bargain roll is gonna happen. If it's important to you that your character is a functioning addict, then now is the time to Excellency your Resolve and whatnot. Simply wanting the character to be a functioning addict isn't enough to resist the temptation if you haven't built the character to be able to. Much like you can't block attacks simply by saying &quot;my character is a deadly warrior, so this attack is insufficient to hit him&quot; (I know that example is a bit extreme, but you get the point).</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the point you are driving at, and I think this is the most reasonably phrased argument yet.<br /> <br /> But even addicts aren't meaningfully tempted by every offer that comes their way.<br /> <br /> Who decides if my character is meaningfully tempted?<br /> <br /> I say, I the player who made the character, decides what they want and crave.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that the ST should say &quot;nah man, you're a junkie that means you're tempted&quot;? Because that's not how Flaws work. Or how the Red Rule works. Or how Persuade, which has to hit an Intimacy, works.<br /> <br /> If I build my character with Integrity 5 does that mean I can say I'm not even tempted, or I am tempted by ST fiat regardless and Resolve is my only resistance to temptation?<br /> <br /> What if Oscar isn't a drug addict? Can Sally still tempt him with opium? Going back to the Ask A Question example, can Sally tempt Opium Oscar with a pair or warm socks?<br /> <br /> Someone has to decide whether the offer is sufficient, no matter how we're defining sufficient. Who is making this call?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:03:57-07:00","id":1402801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402799#post1402799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the point you are driving at, and I think this is the most reasonably phrased argument yet.<br /> <br /> But even addicts aren't meaningfully tempted by every offer that comes their way.<br /> <br /> Who decides if my character is meaningfully tempted?<br /> <br /> I say, I the player who made the character, decides what they want and crave.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that the ST should say &quot;nah man, you're a junkie that means you're tempted&quot;? Because that's not how Flaws work. Or how the Red Rule works. Or how Persuade, which has to hit an Intimacy, works.<br /> <br /> If I build my character with Integrity 5 does that mean I can say I'm not even tempted, or I am tempted by ST fiat regardless and Resolve is my only resistance to temptation?<br /> <br /> What if Oscar isn't a drug addict? Can Sally still tempt him with opium?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've stated in each of my posts so far that the player who made the character should decide, I agree with you entirely on that.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately &quot;being meaningfully tempted&quot; is a huge grey area - the addict with a Minor Flaw won't need to apply resolve nearly as often as one with a Defining Flaw, but even the one with a Defining Flaw may not need a roll to refuse if you're asking them to kill their child in return for a dose. Since Bargains don't have clear rules like the Intimacy system there's no clear way to objectively define the different &quot;degrees&quot; of how tempted your character might be by any given offer, so the character's player is gonna have to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:05:28-07:00","id":1402802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1402754#post1402754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who decides if what is being offered in the Bargain is sufficient?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally it\u2019s something that the Storyteller and the Player would agree on, or even in this case just the Storyteller if it\u2019s an NPC. If you\u2019re going to have a system where Barter is a roll, where there\u2019s a grey area between absolutely no temptation whatsoever, and immediate accepting of the deal with no roll. The player also has a major responsibility here not to abuse that, and that includes the Storyteller. Like you can\u2019t just claim Red Rule any time you want to auto-pass a social influence roll for no other reason than you have Resolve 1 and want to use the Red Rule as a social perfect defense in the social game.<br /> <br /> Obviously you can and should still use it any time you\u2019re uncomfortable, but if you just go \u201coh damn, THIS could be an inconvenient intimacy to have later...but I don\u2019t want to spent a willpower to ignore it. Red Rule!\u201d Then that\u2019s wrong and shouldn\u2019t be done. If your character is desperate to sail the ocean, and is being offered a ship and a crew by somebody who can easily beat her Resolve, that is as dangerous a situation to be in as being locked in combat against a deadly enemy when you yourself are not combat focused at all. In that case you might end up having to enter a decision point to avoid betraying your allies when being offered your heart\u2019s desire by somebody who\u2019s very, very convincing and as a character who\u2019s pretty weak willed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:33:33-07:00","id":1402804,"title":"","content":"Put another way, Exalted has a social system, you don\u2019t have to engage with it, but if you do you don\u2019t actually get to decide what your character does or thinks all the time. If somebody keys off a defining intimacy, you don\u2019t get to decide that their argument is insufficient to sway your character to do this minor task without entering a decision point. If you\u2019re out of willpower then not even then. If nobody thinks it makes sense and nobody is enjoying it you don\u2019t have to engage with it, of course, but that goes for any system too. <br /> <br /> As Epitome said though there\u2019s no firm guidelines in the core as to what should be how temping to who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:39:25-07:00","id":1402806,"title":"","content":"And if the player does keep Red Ruling things, I think you're well within reason as ST to ask, &quot;What WOULD be a reasonable temptation then?&quot; and use that as the offer the NPC makes. However, I realize that is not going to fly at ever table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:45:08-07:00","id":1402807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402806#post1402806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the player does keep Red Ruling things, I think you're well within reason as ST to ask, &quot;What WOULD be a reasonable temptation then?&quot; and use that as the offer the NPC makes. However, I realize that is not going to fly at ever table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Good advice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402801#post1402801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've stated in each of my posts so far that the player who made the character should decide, I agree with you entirely on that.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately &quot;being meaningfully tempted&quot; is a huge grey area - the addict with a Minor Flaw won't need to apply resolve nearly as often as one with a Defining Flaw, but even the one with a Defining Flaw may not need a roll to refuse if you're asking them to kill their child in return for a dose. Since Bargains don't have clear rules like the Intimacy system there's no clear way to objectively define the different &quot;degrees&quot; of how tempted your character might be by any given offer, so the character's player is gonna have to decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I agree with you.<br /> <br /> Where we disagree is how large the grey area is. I can only speak for myself -- I wouldn't want to play a character who had a weakness for drugs if I was never going to give in to that weakness. If someone makes me an offer - a good offer - then I'm taking it, even if it's not &quot;optimal&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;She's offering you drugs if-&quot;<br /> I take the deal.<br /> &quot;You betray the other PCs mwhahaha!&quot;<br /> Did I stutter? Give me the drugs woman!<br /> <br /> In Exalted Flaws only work if they cause you detriment. You WANT to get screwed over by your Flaw. That's why you have a Flaw.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh no! I'm going to spend a Full Excellency so I don't get +2XP!&quot;<br /> <br /> Really? This actually happens in the games you play?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it doesn't but it's well outside of my lived experience.<br /> <br /> If a Guild Merchant wants to hire the PCs to rob a Tomb, he offers them silver and first pick of the treasures and the PCs say &quot;when do we leave&quot;. I don't roll against their Resolve to send them on an adventure.<br /> <br /> And conversely to that if they say &quot;no, that's not good enough&quot;, I let them decide that. Maybe I just have good players?<br /> <br /> Let's close the loop here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grelkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1402252#post1402252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you handle Bargain rolls made against PCs?<br /> <br /> The way Bargain rolls are written, the roll can only be made if something of sufficient value is offered. This makes sense for ST characters - a Matriarch may be forced to exert her will to resist an offer of the marriage of a talented commander into her House, for instance. However, when it comes to PCs, it seems like any player offered something they want would simply accept it without requiring the ST character to roll, while a player who didn't want the thing offered would simply say that it is insufficient and therefore prevent thr ST from making the roll in the first place.<br /> <br /> This assumes a certain level of metagaming, but it seems hard to resolve otherwise without a logn discussion about separating your character from yourself, and a subsequent discussion on how the ST could claim to know characters better than their players do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say: Let players decide if a deal is good enough. Encourage them to accept deals they do think are good enough without rolling. If they player thinks it's a grey area then roll, but if the player says &quot;that offer isn't good enough&quot; then the offer isn't good enough.<br /> <br /> If you have a problematic player, discussing it OOC is a better solution than bludgeoning them with dice rolls. Using the Persuade action to talk them into accepting a deal is a more organic way of getting a trade through as it relies on the character's established Intimacies and the player can't shut it down by saying &quot;That's insufficient&quot;. Supernaturally charming bargainers should use Charms -- like Soul Snaring Pitch to represent their abilities.<br /> <br /> If a player is accepting deals they think are good enough and no-selling deals they (the player) don't think are good enough (for their character) this is the system working as intended. More dice rolls doesn't equate to more drama.<br /> <br /> Do you have any different or additional advice for Grelkis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T08:01:58-07:00","id":1402809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402804#post1402804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If somebody keys off a defining intimacy</div> </div> </div> </div>Then. I. Have. No. Problem. What. So. Ever. With. That. Please. Stop. Conflating. Persuade. With. Bargain. I. Explicitly. Suggested. Using. Persuade. To. Talk. P.Cs. Into. Doing. Things. They. Are. Reluctant. To. Do.<br /> <br /> Because I chose my Intimacies, or developed them naturally in play. I said to the world &quot;my character cares about this&quot;. I decided that my Defining Intimacy defines what my character cares about. If you use something which I've told you I care about to make me act, then I don't have a problem.<br /> <br /> My problem is if the ST says &quot;you DON'T have a Defining Intimacy, but I'm going to make you do this anyway by paying you a talent of silver -- and no, you don't get to decide that this is worth more to you than money because I decide what your character cares about.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> what I object to. No, the ST does not get to decide what a PC cares about. The player decides that.<br /> <br /> The player decides what the character cares about. Cunning NPCs can manipulate the character based on what they care about. That's good gameplay.<br /> <br /> Bargain doesn't care about what you care about. It cares about <i>whether payment is sufficient</i>.<br /> <br /> If the player determines whether payment is sufficient, then I have no problem with Bargain RAW. But the vast majority of the time, whether you are buying a beer or rescuing a Dragon-Blooded from Malfeas, it will be unnecessary to roll to make a deal. Almost every trade or agreement your PCs make will not be rolled as Bargain actions because the PCs will either agree to the terms (&quot;1 kuko for six beers please&quot;) or say payment is insufficient (&quot;no, I won't kill all my friends for six beers&quot;).<br /> <br /> If you're saying the player doesn't get to decide, the ST decides... well enjoy that. You are going to be rolling Bargain a lot more often than I do. Have fun.<br /> <br /> I guess your advice to Grelkis is &quot;Don't let the players have veto power, then your problem is solved&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T08:28:48-07:00","id":1402812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402809#post1402809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I chose my Intimacies, or developed them naturally in play. I said to the world &amp;quot;my character cares about this&amp;quot;. I decided that my Defining Intimacy defines what my character cares about. If you use something which I've told you I care about to make me act, then I don't have a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the bargain roll manipulates an intimacy? \u201cYou don\u2019t want to go tomb raiding for my silver? That\u2019s a shame. You know, I hear that rebellion isn\u2019t doing so well. So many rebellions these days falter due to lack of funding. Running out of food, weapons, bribing officials. Tsk-tsk, poor management all around. Not that any of you care, I\u2019m sure you\u2019re not connected to such a bloody revolution. Oh you\u2019re interested now? *pointedly puts a hand on the chest and drags it back to his side of the table* the tomb, and its prize. Then you get my coin.\u201d<br /> <br /> There we go, now we roll bargain. This isn\u2019t a persuade roll, he\u2019s not telling them go go raid the tomb for their own sake, he wants something out of it. A persuade roll there would be \u201cgo raid that tomb, it\u2019s never been opened and I know you \u2018can\u2019t resist a mystery\u2019 right?\u201d. He\u2019s getting something out of it, it\u2019s a transaction.<br /> <br /> I object to players just being able to say \u201cno he didn\u2019t convince me, no roll.\u201d just because they don\u2019t want to be convinced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T08:49:22-07:00","id":1402813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402807#post1402807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where we disagree is how large the grey area is. I can only speak for myself -- I wouldn't want to play a character who had a weakness for drugs if I was never going to give in to that weakness. If someone makes me an offer - a good offer - then I'm taking it, even if it's not &quot;optimal&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> If a Guild Merchant wants to hire the PCs to rob a Tomb, he offers them silver and first pick of the treasures and the PCs say &quot;when do we leave&quot;. I don't roll against their Resolve to send them on an adventure.<br /> <br /> And conversely to that if they say &quot;no, that's not good enough&quot;, I let them decide that. Maybe I just have good players?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this sidebar about social rules in the corebook is appropriate here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core p.218</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short: Remember that these rules are there to supplement good old-fashioned roleplaying, not to cast a net over it or box it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your table has things covered without ever needing to make Bargain rolls, then there's nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402807#post1402807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any different or additional advice for Grelkis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, seems like good advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T09:53:46-07:00","id":1402817,"title":"","content":"Also just to clarify here, the reason a player might want to not accept that deal is because maybe their rebellion seems to be doing okay, and they\u2019re really hoping to wrap it up soon anyway. The legendary merchant convinced them that they need more coin, in case of an emergency or because so often these things run off schedule, etc. Or you might have a character like this<br /> <br /> Defining tie of Love for sick brother<br /> Major tie of loyalty to circle <br /> <br /> <br /> Then somebody offers you something you thought didn\u2019t exist, a cure for your sick sibling, but you must betray your circle to get it. A character who resists that deal could be planning on just coming back and stealing it later, but the bargain roll is to convince you to take that deal right now, don\u2019t risk failing at your heist, or that I\u2019ll destroy the cure after this meeting, just make the trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T10:09:31-07:00","id":1402821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402812#post1402812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the bargain roll manipulates an intimacy? \u201cYou don\u2019t want to go tomb raiding for my silver? That\u2019s a shame. You know, I hear that rebellion isn\u2019t doing so well. So many rebellions these days falter due to lack of funding. Running out of food, weapons, bribing officials. Tsk-tsk, poor management all around. Not that any of you care, I\u2019m sure you\u2019re not connected to such a bloody revolution. Oh you\u2019re interested now? *pointedly puts a hand on the chest and drags it back to his side of the table* the tomb, and its prize. Then you get my coin.\u201d<br /> <br /> There we go, now we roll bargain. This isn\u2019t a persuade roll, he\u2019s not telling them go go raid the tomb for their own sake, he wants something out of it. A persuade roll there would be \u201cgo raid that tomb, it\u2019s never been opened and I know you \u2018can\u2019t resist a mystery\u2019 right?\u201d. He\u2019s getting something out of it, it\u2019s a transaction.<br /> <br /> I object to players just being able to say \u201cno he didn\u2019t convince me, no roll.\u201d just because they don\u2019t want to be convinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the player no-selling it?<br /> <br /> If they just don't want to play Exalted, then rolling against their character's Resolve isn't going to help the game. You just get a reluctant player feeling railroaded through your plot. It's not legitimate to say &quot;no you're not playing properly and I'm rolling 15 dice with ten automatic non-Charm successes anyway! Ha! I convinced you!&quot; You need to discuss it OOC. Honestly, it's something you should have discussed on Session 0.<br /> <br /> If they have a legitimate reason to think that the Bargain action is insufficient despite hitting an Intimacy (e.g. they have Defining support for the revolution, but are pretty sure robbing this tomb is a suicide mission and they're not convinced that a chest of silver <i>maybe</i> is going to help), then the player gets to no-sell the roll. Just like you can't use the Defining Intimacy of Revolution on any random Persuade roll -- the roll has to actually, legitimately call on the Intimacy in question. You can't say &quot;You love your wife, eh? Well there's nothing wives love more than regicide...&quot;<br /> <br /> If the player does think the offer is sufficient and wants funds for the rebellion... why are they rolling? Go rob that tomb!<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, it would be my expectation that if someone is offered a Bargain that aligns with their Intimacies, the player accept the Bargain. If it's a grey area (perhaps because there are Intimacies supporting and opposing the Bargain), then maybe roll for it. But I wouldn't expect that to happen more than a couple of times a Story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T10:23:57-07:00","id":1402827,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s for exactly the same reason that Persuade exists. If I can just say \u201cMy character can\u2019t resist a mystery, he\u2019s telling me the tomb is mysterious, so I\u2019m going for it!\u201d Then that\u2019s it and there\u2019s no need to bust out the system. If it\u2019s dangerous, and I\u2019ve heard that actually it has been broken into before and there\u2019s nothing in it anyway, and I might want to go do something else that\u2019s also kind of pressing right now, then the silver tongued devil whispering in my ear is what convinces me. He uses words to fill my character\u2019s mind with visions of lost lore and treasures, all while soothing my reservations by saying how the people who supposedly broke in before were simple folk who couldn\u2019t possibly have understood what they saw or even gotten past the outer door. <br /> <br /> When it\u2019s a bargain roll the roll is there to convince you to take this deal, you need it, you can only get it from me, and it has to be here and now. You think the rebellion\u2019s war chest is doing fine, but is it? You\u2019re dealing with rebels, they don\u2019t necessarily all think stealing is wrong what if they start skimming the war chest? What if mistakes get made? It happens so often. Building fears in you, anxiety, filling your head with visions of running out of cash two steps before the finish line, and having your revolution crushed and the oppression return with a literal vengeance. This, though, this silver alone will fund your armies through months, maybe a full year, of incursions. <br /> <br /> Do you ACTUALLY need it? Maybe not, but that dude sure made a good case for it. If r beat your resolve anyway. If not you\u2019re free to shrug and say \u201cI think we\u2019ll be fine, thanks.\u201d and walk away","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T10:32:10-07:00","id":1402830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402817#post1402817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also just to clarify here, the reason a player might want to not accept that deal is because maybe their rebellion seems to be doing okay, and they\u2019re really hoping to wrap it up soon anyway. The legendary merchant convinced them that they need more coin, in case of an emergency or because so often these things run off schedule, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not legitimately tagging the Intimacy. No sell.<br /> <br /> I mean, for meta reasons, I would expect the PCs to go along with it. Because plot. And if a player wasn't convinced but accepted they were convincable, then sure, roll.<br /> <br /> But as written, that's &quot;Your wife loves onions: let's go kill the king!&quot; I'd no-sell that in a heart-beat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402817#post1402817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you might have a character like this<br /> <br /> Defining tie of Love for sick brother<br /> Major tie of loyalty to circle <br /> <br /> <br /> Then somebody offers you something you thought didn\u2019t exist, a cure for your sick sibling, but you must betray your circle to get it. A character who resists that deal could be planning on just coming back and stealing it later, but the bargain roll is to convince you to take that deal right now, don\u2019t risk failing at your heist, or that I\u2019ll destroy the cure after this meeting, just make the trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's almost certainly legitimate. I still say the player gets veto if they really want to -- but this is exactly the sort of thing that might call for a Bargain roll. If a player tried to no-sell this, we'd be having that OOC conversation about playing in good faith, and maybe a rejiggle of the PCs Intimacies. And if they tried this more than a couple of times, I'd drop them from the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402827#post1402827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Building fears in you, anxiety, filling your head with visions of running out of cash two steps before the finish line, and having your revolution crushed and the oppression return with a literal vengeance. </div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an Inspire roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402827#post1402827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you ACTUALLY need it? Maybe not, but that dude sure made a good case for it. If r beat your resolve anyway. If not you\u2019re free to shrug and say \u201cI think we\u2019ll be fine, thanks.\u201d and walk away</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever worked in sales? Because that happens A LOT.<br /> <br /> And you haven't beaten my Resolve because I've told you the offer isn't sufficient before you've rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T10:55:59-07:00","id":1402835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402830#post1402830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not legitimately tagging the Intimacy. No sell.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it not tagging the intimacy? I\u2019m telling you that this money is going to be super helpful to your cause. You didn\u2019t think you needed it before you came in here, possibly/probably because you legitimately didn\u2019t, but after hearing my pitch, well now that I mention it you have seen some people eyeing that war chest a bit too close for comfort.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402830#post1402830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have you ever worked in sales? Because that happens A LOT.<br /> <br /> And you haven't beaten my Resolve because I've told you the offer isn't sufficient before you've rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have worked in sales and, although I\u2019m not proud of it, oh better believe I sold people things they didn\u2019t want for prices that make no sense when you really look at it. I tried to avoid it as much as possible and instead giving people what they needed, including sometimes sending them to other stores, but sometimes I got pressured into pushing for a sale that was not at all in the customer\u2019s best interest. Extended service plans especially, basically pay 1/3 again the cost of your device for a limited warranty that covers very few things the manufacturer doesn\u2019t, and conveniently runs out at just about the crest of the hill where stuff actually starts breaking down normally. <br /> <br /> I did it by saying stuff like \u201chow annoying is it when in sixteen months, just after the damn manufacturers warranty runs out, or if it\u2019s starting to get a bit sluggish and you have no idea why, and don\u2019t want to come to us for a diagnostic? This is a three year plan, covering everything the manufacturer does and more, and any time at all when you feel something might be wrong, take it in to our tech support department and we will give you a FREE diagnostic* for as long as you own the plan. You can even take it home today, discuss it with your partner, and if you don\u2019t like it come in before the return policy is up and return just the plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> Imagine how bad it would feel to have it break, think of how freeing it is to know you can always come to us, even if you never use it, you\u2019re paying like 1/6th the cost of this machine every year for the simple peace of mind that you will always have it.**<br /> <br /> That\u2019s how you sell somebody some useless crap they will likely not need for more than it\u2019s worth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *all our tech department diagnostics are basically free anyway, if there is a problem and you pay to have it fixed we deduct the cost of the diagnostic from your final repair bill.<br /> <br /> **unless you care about your data because 50% of issues are HDD related and we charge out the ass for recovery fees. We warranty your hardware, not software***.<br /> <br /> ***Because NOBODY warrantees software! You can\u2019t! Once it\u2019s gone, it\u2019s gone, it\u2019s literally impossible to contractually obligate us to fix your data.****<br /> <br /> ****just don\u2019t think about how it could contractually obligate is to attempt recovery","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:53:28-07:00","id":1402847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402835#post1402835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it not tagging the intimacy? I\u2019m telling you that this money is going to be super helpful to your cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But it's not.<br /> <br /> If I have a Defining Tie of Love for my husband, you could say that robbing this tomb will make him love me more. But, you know, it won't. And there's no reason why I'd believe you.<br /> <br /> If the rebellion actually was having money trouble, or you Inspired doubt and were trying to leverage that, then sure. Or if you Instilled a new Principle or Tie. Or if you Puersauded me based off other Intimacies to go out and get more money.<br /> <br /> But you can't just say &quot;this random unrelated thing will vaguely help your intimacy (even though it won't)&quot;. At least according to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1178525#post1178525\">Word of Vance</a> (and, you know, common sense).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T12:01:45-07:00","id":1402849,"title":"","content":"There are multiple entire professions whose description is \u201cConvince you that a deal is good.\u201d If your character has no middle ground for them to work with between \u201cWill 100% take that deal without a second thought\u201d and \u201cAbsolutely will never take that deal no matter what\u201d then you\u2019re acting in bad faith. Full stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T12:02:33-07:00","id":1402850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402847#post1402847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have a Defining Tie of Love for my husband, you could say that robbing this tomb will make him love me more. But, you know, it won't. <b>And there's no reason why I'd believe you.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a heck of an assertion to make <i>before the pitch has even been made</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T13:09:26-07:00","id":1402856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402850#post1402850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a heck of an assertion to make <i>before the pitch has even been made</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not based on anything.<br /> <br /> If my husband has previously expressed admiration for grave robbers, or there's prior social rolls to sow that seed, then sure.<br /> <br /> But you can't just randomly fluff an outright lie to appeal to any intimacy you like.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your favourite color is orange. Buy this orange shirt.&quot;<br /> My favourite color is blue.<br /> &quot;Nah bro, I rolled 12 successes on my Bargain roll exploiting your Intimacy of 'I only wear clothes of my favourite color'.&quot;<br /> <br /> You cannot pick an Intimacy at random and claim whatever you are trying to do keys off that Intimacy when it <i>in no way</i> keys off that Intimacy as you outright lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402849#post1402849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are multiple entire professions whose description is \u201cConvince you that a deal is good.\u201d If your character has no middle ground for them to work with between \u201cWill 100% take that deal without a second thought\u201d and \u201cAbsolutely will never take that deal no matter what\u201d then you\u2019re acting in bad faith. Full stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to seperate player and character.<br /> <br /> My character is going to agonize over betraying his friends for opium. But there's no need to introduce a dice roll here, because I, the player, want the 2 Flaw XP.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if there's two contrary things a character cares about, it's conceivable that there's a middle ground for convincing here. Or if you don't care about something one way or the other.<br /> <br /> But within the context of rules for player characters in an RPG, where the rules explicitly state that a character has to think a Bargain is worthwhile in order for it to succeed? I don't buy it. Unless you want to Inspire, Instill or Persuade beforehand, you're not convincing someone with your Bargain roll unless you're offering something they want. It's not bad faith to say &quot;no, my character doesn't want that&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-14-2020, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T21:08:33-07:00","id":1402910,"title":"","content":"Remind me, is Flaw XP gained on top of Splat and Session XP? <br /> <br /> If so, that\u2019s an interesting incentive thing (like in Savage Worlds where the ST could offer you Bennies for screwing up your character/party).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T21:50:44-07:00","id":1402913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402856#post1402856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's not based on anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cI spoke to your husband and he wants you to do this.\u201d<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re totally confident that your husband would never ever actually ask you to rob a tomb then congrats on the -5 dice penalty that page 227 says I take to try and convince you otherwise, but if I still beat your Resolve with what I have left after that then it\u2019s still decision point time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not bad faith to say &amp;quot;no, my character doesn't want that&amp;quot;. </div> </div> </div>It is the way you\u2019re saying it. There\u2019s nothing about a quid pro quo that turns on some kind of magical \u201cCan\u2019t be changed\u201d switched in people\u2019s minds; if someone can be talked into things then they can be talked into paying $19.99 for five feet of Flex Tape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T04:15:45-07:00","id":1402928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402913#post1402913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cI spoke to your husband and he wants you to do this.\u201d<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re totally confident that your husband would never ever actually ask you to rob a tomb then congrats on the -5 dice penalty that page 227 says I take to try and convince you otherwise, but if I still beat your Resolve with what I have left after that then it\u2019s still decision point time.</div> </div> </div> </div>People aren't robots running &quot;does this speech hit my Intimacy switch&quot;. The social system doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is the way you\u2019re saying it. There\u2019s nothing about a quid pro quo that turns on some kind of magical \u201cCan\u2019t be changed\u201d switched in people\u2019s minds; if someone can be talked into things then they can be talked into paying $19.99 for five feet of Flex Tape. </div> </div> </div>Sure. If you want flex tape, a good bargain roll can sell you five feet for twenty bucks.<br /> <br /> But as Resources is abstracted, I say just let your PC get gouged and grumble about it IC.<br /> <br /> But you can't just sell flex tape to some random PC who doesn't want it and has no need for it. Not without having several social rolls in advance to set up a need or Charms.<br /> <br /> &gt;buy my flex tape, $19.99<br /> <br /> I don't need flex tape. No sell.<br /> <br /> &gt;FLEX TAPE is a super strong rubberized waterproof tape that can patch bond seal and repair virtually everything! FLEX TAPE is specially formulated with a thick flexible rubberized backing that conforms to any shape or object! FLEX TAPE can be applied hot or cold wet or dry even underwater!<br /> <br /> I still don't need Flex Tape. No sell. (And apologies to any of you who read the sales pitch for Flex Tape and immediately bought some.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T04:40:44-07:00","id":1402930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402910#post1402910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me, is Flaw XP gained on top of Splat and Session XP?<br /> <br /> If so, that\u2019s an interesting incentive thing (like in Savage Worlds where the ST could offer you Bennies for screwing up your character/party).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's part of Splat XP - you get the expression 2xp for either doing a range of things with an intimacy or being impeded by a flaw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T05:28:46-07:00","id":1402933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402793#post1402793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who decides if Oscar is in a good mood or a bad mood? Who decides if Oscar is going to step up?</div> </div> </div> </div>The player decides if Oscar <i>wants</i> to step up. The dice decide if Oscar <i>does</i> step up. If they didn't, the player might as well decide everything. <br /> Why does the player then not get to decide whether his sword strike hits that death knight? How dare you force upon the player the decision of having missed his attack?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I contend that the player decides what their character does. The player decides if they're going to rescue the princess or guard the door or go get high. </div> </div> </div>The player decides what his character <i>wants</i> to do. If the player gave his character a flaw of drug addiction, it really isn't too much abuse to then ask him to periodically roll for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Oscar isn't a character in a book. And he's not a real person. He's MY character. I make the decisions for my character.<br /> <br /> In combat, I decide whether I take an Aim action or an Attack action. You don't get to say &quot;Aiming is unrealistic, you have to Attack&quot;. I get to choose what my character does.<br /> <br /> If you insult my character, I decide whether I laugh it off or challenge you to a duel. That's the point of me playing. </div> </div> </div>But if you take the aim action, and then attack, you have to roll your attack to see if it hits. Why is it so outrageous to you that a character with intimacies that might make him a bit of a choleric twat might need to roll to stay cool and laugh off that insult?<br /> Exalted gives you all the tools, if you want to be cool as a cucumber then give yourself an intimacy that makes insults roll off you, if you want a hothead, have an intimacy that makes it hard for you to ignore insults.<br /> <br /> I get where you're arguing from and you're not wrong, I just don't get why you insist on skipping this huge middle ground between your position and the straw man opposition of ST dictatorship ruining your fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for &quot;following the rules&quot; the rules say, in black and white, that the offer must be &quot;worth the difficulty or danger of the task you\u2019re asking him to perform&quot;. I am advocating that you follow the rules -- you must offer something which is worth it.<br /> <br /> The question is, who decides what's worth it?<br /> <br /> If the player decides that an offer is worth it, just accept the offer. If the player decides it isn't worth it, then <i>according to the rules</i>, the Bargain fails.<br /> <br /> If the ST decides that Oscar is having a bad day and the opium hit seems worth it to him, then sure that blows the middle ground a mile wide. But I contend that this shouldn't happen -- the player should decide whether Oscar is having a bad day. </div> </div> </div>Maybe my argument for middle grounds was too much of a middle ground. I agree that the ST just saying &quot;you're having a bad day, sucks for you&quot; sounds like the ST being a jerk, but let's just pretend I phrased this more elegantly, and we can probably agree that there might be days where Oscar might say yes, and days where he might say no, right?<br /> I feel like rolling dice is an OK abstraction on deciding what kind of day you're role playing at this instant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oscar and Sally don't exist. John, the player, and Chesire, the ST, exist. Oscar doesn't get a say: John decides what is and isn't important to Oscar, and John decides if Oscar is going to step up or shirk off. Because Oscar isn't real. Oscar doesn't want to descend into the Labyrinth and foil the plots of the thousand year old Deathlords. Oscar doesn't <i>want</i> anything. Oscar exists purely as a vessel for me to tell a story. I invented Oscar. I made him a drug addict. I made him a functioning drug addict. I know exactly how strong his addiction is, because I'm the one who invented him. I know how much he cares about guarding a door, because I'm the one who decided he cares about guarding the door. I should be the one who decides if he cares more about guarding the door or getting high. </div> </div> </div>I feel like you absolutely get to decide all this at character creation, and your intimacies should reflect that. But if there is no mechanism of conflict you accept as overriding your player agency, then you might as well not play. Oscars struggle with addiction is not a worthwhile flaw, or interesting character trait, if it is impossible to leverage for conflict.<br /> And to put on my pretentious RPG nerd hat: if you created Oscar with love and passion, then it should feel as if Oscar <i>does </i>want things, and it should immediately resonate with you what that is. And if that results in you being dead-sure that Oscar doesn't take a hit of opium, then just spend a point of willpower, that's what it's for.<br /> <br /> Oscar is treated as a character in the story with as much agency as any non-trivial character, whether PC or NPC, for story integrity (your mileage might vary by table) - and you can certainly argue with your ST about what a sufficient amount of temptation is to force a roll, and I certainly think an ST who is making you roll to do incredibly dumb shit vs very little reward is abusing the bargaining system, I agree with you there.<br /> But I feel like you're making this more absolute than it has to be. And if ST and Player can't agree, the player can always spend willpower, which is exactly the resource the game gave us to have characters not do stuff they might reasonably be doing.<br /> <br /> And if your Oscar isn't that hardcore of an addict, or still has intimacies besides getting high that are strong, maybe even a defining sense of duty, that bargain roll will be quite tough to succeed at anyway. Bargain rolls aren't supposed to be auto-win, they're supposed to let you trade something in place of leveraging an intimacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For NPCs, this is a completely different equation. For NPCs, the ST has discretion and the middle ground is truly enormous.<br /> <br /> If Sally is a PC and Oscar is an NPC, then roll away.<br /> <br /> But there's a fundamental difference between NPCs and PCs.<br /> <br /> Are you honestly saying that I shouldn't be allowed to say &quot;My character, Oscar, doesn't think Sally's offer to let her pass for a hit of opium is worth the danger that puts him in&quot;? You're saying I don't get to make that decision for my character? Who does get to make it? </div> </div> </div>I'm saying if your character has a Flaw of opium addiction, there might be a worthwhile discussion about whether he really doesn't want that opium. But TBH as you describe the situation, Oscar <b>does</b> care about the door, and it <b>does</b> put him in danger, so the bargain action would be asking for quite a serious task and might be opposed by strong intimacies, so the roll to convince Oscar might be really hard.<br /> And even if it succeeds, you can spend some of Oscar's willpower for him.<br /> I feel this is okay.<br /> I feel this is something the ST might rule on, yes.<br /> Because if you get to decide all aspects of conflict just because they involve your character, you're not playing anymore, you're writing fan fiction.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the situation is really this straw-man-y and it really is a <i>tiny bit of Opium</i> which is valued against <i>a life-threatening task opposed by Defining or Major Intimacies</i>, then this is just the ST abusing you, John, the player, and using Oscar, the character to do it. That's a shitty ST, and not really a problem of the mechanics, or the social influence engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T05:58:23-07:00","id":1402936,"title":"","content":"I feel like I don't <i>meaningfully</i> disagree with what you've written <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar903_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"903\" data-vbnamecard=\"903\">Cheshire Cat</a>, and I'm disinclined to argue the minutia.<br /> <br /> My point is you have to offer something the character wants for a Bargain action to succeed. Charms like &quot;Finding the Water's Depths&quot; can tell you what the character wants. You can't just offer whatever you like -- it has to be something the character wants.<br /> <br /> There <i>is</i> a middle ground where it's equivocal whether a character wants something or not, and I'm fine with letting the dice decide in such a situation. But, in my experience, people take deals that they think are worthwhile -- that's the point of making a deal.<br /> <br /> If you don't think the ST should bludgeon the PCs, and you're happy with the principle of offering something the PC wants, then I've got no beef.<br /> <br /> For the sake of my sanity, let's close the loop here:<br /> <br /> Grelkis asks what stops the players no-selling NPC bargain rolls. My reading of your post is that you believe the ST should rule whether the offer is sufficient, not the player. Is that a fair reading? (It's not my opinion, but it's a valid opinion.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T06:04:30-07:00","id":1402938,"title":"","content":"Yeah I felt like most of our disagreement was due to me not phrasing my previous argument as elegantly as it could've been, and beyond that it all seems very granular, so let's just agree to 90% agree and not sweat the 10%.<br /> <br /> Edit: I might've also shot past your point a bit where you elaborate on the point that the contention might be about what the character wants, which I kind of assumed was a given. So yeah, I could've wasted less of both of our time. Thanks for taking the time anyway. And on the 10% we disagree on, I hope I gave some food for thought.<br /> <br /> To the point:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402936#post1402936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grelkis asks what stops the players no-selling NPC bargain rolls. My reading of your post is that you believe the ST should rule whether the offer is sufficient, not the player. Is that a fair reading? (It's not my opinion, but it's a valid opinion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To make it very granular: it should be collaborative.<br /> In principle I agree with you that the player should decide, or rather frame the issue.<br /> But I here see the potential of abuse of a player not wanting to &quot;lose&quot; anything, and just no-selling anything the ST/NPC offers up, so I feel if it comes to a meaningful disagreement the ST should have the last word, so a character's flaws/intimacies/desires can actually at some point be leveraged.<br /> <br /> So yeah it's a fair reading, the ST should have the last word.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: I feel like we see similar problems of abuse, and I've seen players try to be invincible more, and you've seen STs being antagonistic more - might this just be the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":903,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","user":"Cheshire Cat","date":". 07-15-2020, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T09:46:48-07:00","id":1402960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402928#post1402928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People aren't robots running &amp;quot;does this speech hit my Intimacy switch&amp;quot;. The social system doesn't work like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Persuade actions work <i>exactly</i> like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you can't just sell flex tape to some random PC who doesn't want it and has no need for it. Not without having several social rolls in advance to set up a need or Charms. </div> </div> </div><i>Exactly</i> wrong again, instilling \u201cI want Flex Tape\u201d first is what a bargain action <i>specifically does not require</i>. Sure I could do so anyway for the -1 Resolve if I wanted to, but sawing this boat in half to convince you why Flex Tape is acceptable compensation for your parting with $19.99 works perfectly well as the bargain stunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402936#post1402936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is you have to offer something the character wants for a Bargain action to succeed. Charms like &amp;quot;Finding the Water's Depths&amp;quot; can tell you what the character wants. You can't just offer whatever you like -- it has to be something the character wants.<br /> <br /> There <i>is</i> a middle ground where it's equivocal whether a character wants something or not, and I'm fine with letting the dice decide in such a situation. But, in my experience, people take deals that they think are worthwhile -- that's the point of making a deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mention that Charm, because that middle ground is precisely what it finds (as opposed to Knowing the Soul\u2019s Price which finds the offer they\u2019d accept without a roll). Where you\u2019re going wrong is thinking that that middle ground is some narrow sweet spot that\u2019s a crapshoot to guess at. It\u2019s not. All the examples of unacceptable bargains are egregious lowball offers like trying to bribe an aristocrat with a piece of fruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T10:51:41-07:00","id":1402965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402960#post1402960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Persuade actions work <i>exactly</i> like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> I refer you to the Orichalcum and Storyteller's rules on page 182. These set the tone of how the rules should be interpreted. Then there's &quot;Roleplaying: A Reminder&quot; on page 218. <br /> <br /> Further, you are conflating the penalties for Instilling a hard to accept belief with Persuade's need to be supported by an Intimacy. The rules for Persuade and Instill can be found on page 215/6.<br /> <br /> Plus, straight up, the person in charge of developing the rules of the game disagrees with you. Like, damn, people should feel free to argue with me but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page546#post1178525\">I literally posted Vance explaining that this line of reasoning is wrong</a>.<br /> <br /> Do you want to quote a rules example or something that supports the idea that you don't need a supporting Intimacy for a Persuade action? Because I absolutely tell you now -- a Persuade action automatically fails if it's not supported by a sufficiently strong Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Exactly</i> wrong again, instilling \u201cI want Flex Tape\u201d first is what a bargain action <i>specifically does not require</i>. </div> </div> </div>You don't need to Instill an Intimacy, IF someone thinks your Flex Tape is worth $20. If they don't think your Flex Tape is worth $20, your Bargain automatically fails. The full text of the Bargain action is in the OP, but here's a snippet:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>you must</b> offer a bribe, gift, <br /> or favor that the character you\u2019re <br /> convincing believes is worth the dif-<br /> ficulty or danger of the task you\u2019re <br /> asking him to perform.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't see how you can read that and think you can just offer whatever you like. You have to offer something people think is worth the cost. That's the point of this thread -- who decides what's worth the cost.<br /> <br /> The rules aren't &quot;you may offer anything you like if you roll really well&quot;. The rules are you must offer a worthwhile trade.<br /> <br /> That's why we have Charms for stuff like hiding a clause in a deal or selling your castle for a horse.<br /> <br /> They don't have to want Flex Tape. They have to think your Flex Tape is worth $20. If they don't think the tape is worth $20, it doesn't matter how many successes you roll -- your Bargain action fails.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Funny you mention that Charm, because that middle ground is precisely what it finds (as opposed to Knowing the Soul\u2019s Price which finds the offer they\u2019d accept without a roll). Where you\u2019re going wrong is thinking that that middle ground is some narrow sweet spot that\u2019s a crapshoot to guess at. It\u2019s not. All the examples of unacceptable bargains are egregious lowball offers like trying to bribe an aristocrat with a piece of fruit. </div> </div> </div>Sure you can guess what a character considers worth the cost. But you have to offer something worth the cost. That's literally what the rules say. Sure, offering an apple to a noble isn't going to be as convincing as offering one to a beggar. But that doesn't mean you can offer anything you like to anyone for any task.<br /> <br /> My argument isn't &quot;you should never make Bargain rolls&quot;. It's that the game is obviously skewed to assymetry between PCs and NPCs -- and PCs generally won't require Bargain rolls to accept deals where sufficient payment is being offered. Even if the system entitles them to apply Resolve against the deal, PCs (hungry for adventure, greedy for coin and eager for plot) will generally go along with what's offered. And if they don't, it's usually because you're trying to screw them by offering apples to nobles -- offer the characters something they want, or break out the Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-15-2020, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:57:12-07:00","id":1403010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402856#post1402856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's not based on anything.<br /> <br /> If my husband has previously expressed admiration for grave robbers, or there's prior social rolls to sow that seed, then sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I think this is where we're having issues.<br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting that in a complete vacuum you should be able to just deploy a dozen successes and convince anyone to take a deal regardless of context. Maybe you do want to first inspire doubt before going in for the bargain roll. The point is that the player is nearly 100% certain that the rebellion does not in any way need those funds, but their character who's getting their Resolve beaten is getting taken for a ride.<br /> <br /> There should be the option for your character to get screwed in a deal, just like your character can fail a balance check, or get hit with a decisive attack, or have their weapon stolen from them. You don't need to get screwed in a deal by having some worthless trash offered to you. Maybe you just don't need what they're selling, but they make you feel like you need it. It's valuable, just not to your character really, until they get sold on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Arguably it's less invasive than a standard persuade roll, because at least you're getting something out of it. If you're being convinced to go fight a war in exchange for Stormcaller, you're coming out of that with Stormcaller. If you're being convinced to go fight a war by leveraging an intimacy, you're just going off to go fight a war with nothing in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 07-15-2020, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T00:44:30-07:00","id":1403058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1403010#post1403010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you do want to first inspire doubt before going in for the bargain roll. [...]<br /> <br /> Maybe you just don't need what they're selling, but they make you feel like you need it. It's valuable, just not to your character really, until they get sold on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1402299#post1402299\">I advocated pretty much exactly this in my second post</a>.<br /> <br /> If you make a character want a thing, then they want that thing when you attempt a Bargain roll. No contest, Your Honour -- if they want the thing they want the thing.<br /> <br /> If you took my post to mean that if they want the thing then they can't be offered anything in exchange, then I apologise unreservedly for the miscommunication. <i>Of course</i> you may still trade if you'd rather get something for your efforts.<br /> <br /> I decide if my character only has one hand. You can't decide I have one hand by fiat. You can't say &quot;I made a Withering attack that beat your Parry by 6 so now you have one hand&quot;. But you absolutely could use Charms or some custom Gambit, or force a crippling injury that causes me to lose a hand. That's <i>never</i> been in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T11:42:08-07:00","id":1407340,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the necro but I finally got around to reading through this thread.<br /> <br /> Having read through the whole thing so far I'm generally more inclined to come down on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a>'s side of things, mainly due to this particular extract:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402809#post1402809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because I chose my Intimacies, or developed them naturally in play. I said to the world &quot;my character cares about this&quot;. I decided that my Defining Intimacy defines what my character cares about. If you use something which I've told you I care about to make me act, then I don't have a problem.<br /> <br /> My problem is if the ST says &quot;you DON'T have a Defining Intimacy, but I'm going to make you do this anyway by paying you a talent of silver -- and no, you don't get to decide that this is worth more to you than money because I decide what your character cares about.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> what I object to. No, the ST does not get to decide what a PC cares about. The player decides that.<br /> <br /> The player decides what the character cares about. Cunning NPCs can manipulate the character based on what they care about. That's good gameplay.<br /> <br /> Bargain doesn't care about what you care about. It cares about <i>whether payment is sufficient</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to me to me encompass the whole problem quite nicely: bargain supposedly works with reference to a character's desires, but for some reason ignores the system we already have in place (intimacies) and instead appeals to some nebulous set of motivations that exist beyond them. As pointed out above, though, the players have already declared what their characters care about by setting intimacies, so appealing to something outside those intimacies is meaningless because you're appealing to something explicitly outside what motivates their character.<br /> <br /> To resolve this, I'd be inclined to do away with bargain all together and say that all dramatic conflict with respect to manipulating character motivations be carried out with persuade, instill and inspire actions. Bargain actions would then be a mechanically indistinguishable version of the persuade action, based in-universe on offering something to allow someone to satisfy an intimacy, as opposed to being based on rhetorical skill.or evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24811-grelkis","user":"Grelkis","date":".  Corrected typos 08-10-2020, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24811-grelkis","name":"Grelkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T17:05:08-07:00","id":1407399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grelkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407340#post1407340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to me to me encompass the whole problem quite nicely: bargain supposedly works with reference to a character's desires, but for some reason ignores the system we already have in place (intimacies) and instead appeals to some nebulous set of motivations that exist beyond them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I contest this point, bargain actions do not necessarily rely on nebulous motivations outside of intimacies, and furthermore even when a specific intimacy is not being relied upon directly in the bargain action, intimacies both penalize and boost resolve against that bargain action, giving added defenses and weaknesses based on what your character really cares about. Example:<br /> <br /> <br /> Dave the Daring is a Dawn with the following intimacies:<br /> <br /> Defining &quot;I will get my sister's soul back from the Necromancer Galvan and put her to rest.&quot;<br /> Major Necromancer Galvan (Hatred)<br /> Major Kingdom of Swadia (Loyalty)<br /> Minor Cousin Dilliam (Disgust)<br /> <br /> <br /> Another character Swan the Suave is a legendary information broker, if you think you've got a secret, there's a 50% chance he already knows it, and a 100% chance that, given the opportunity, he's going to use it. Now, Swan hates Swadia. He thinks it sucks and wants it roughed up a little. Not destroyed, just, you know, a couple raiding parties here, a burned grainery there, that kind of thing. Sadly, Dave the Daring protects Swadia loyally.<br /> <br /> At this moment, he has no ability to convince Dave to sit this one out, a major request. There is no intimacy of Dave's that can be manipulated to get him to bench himself and not come to the aid of Swadia when it calls after him to fix their bandit problem. Persuade, as an action, is useless here. On the other hand, Swan knows the location of the Necromancer Galvan's hidden fortress, and what's more, he even knows that the soul of Dave's sister is being kept there. That information isn't free though. He wants it? He has to sit out this battle.<br /> <br /> Now, Dave's player might think that Dave is pretty awesome, and even though he might not know Galvan's location right now, he'll eventually find it, so he doesn't want to take this deal. He'll protect Swadia and just keep looking for Galvan's fortress on his own, screw this Swan guy. I am arguing that Swan here gets to roll against Dave's Resolve to see if he will take the deal, he can't just no-sell it because you get to no-sell bargain rolls. That's not my houserule or anything, that's what I think the text of the rules right now lays out.<br /> <br /> Also kind of key here, the value, or validity, of what's being offered isn't always represented fairly. Swan may actually know nothing about Galvan, except that Dave hates him and he has Dave's sister, depending on how reasonable it is that he does he's going to take a dice penalty to the bargain roll. There will be serious consequences for him if he does lie, but he can <i>attempt </i>to lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If we want to talk about bargaining for money or baubles or something, we're going to have to take a bit of a step back from epic heroes bargaining for the soul of the only person they've ever loved. I'm not saying that anyone should just be able to pull out some amount of silver and get to roll to get anything they want out of it. If somebody is offering your character a significant percentage of their current wealth to do something like take a detour, or deliver a package or something, that's worth rolling for.<br /> <br /> Like if somebody offered to clear all my student debt, and a bonus $20,000 cash in exchange for sleeping on my couch for a week, I'm suspicious as fuck about that and won't want to do it. On the other hand I really do feel like if that same scenario were in an Exalted game I was running, an incredible force of personality and charisma should be able to tempt me to do it. <i>Especially </i>if she lies about it. &quot;Hey I'm a secret billionaire, not multi-billionaire but, you know, pretty good. This money is almost literally pocket change for me, but I'm also hiding from my ex-husband who wants me dead. Gimme a week here in this random house that I picked, don't tell anyone, he has friends in the police force, and I'll be out of your hair with you that much richer.&quot; At that point? I'm convinced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:08:21-07:00","id":1407407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1402965#post1402965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want to quote a rules example or something that supports the idea that you don't need a supporting Intimacy for a Persuade action?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Are you screwing with me here because I can quote how we were explicitly talking the whole time about a character <i>with</i> a supporting Intimacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T00:06:01-07:00","id":1407457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407407#post1407407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Are you screwing with me here because I can quote how we were explicitly talking the whole time about a character <i>with</i> a supporting Intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read the post where Vance says &quot;no you can't just pick any intimacy and claim it supports your action when it doesn't&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because you can't just pick any random intimacy and bullshit that it supports your action when it does not.<br /> <br /> Vance's post is right here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1178525#post1178525\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...25#post1178525</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T06:44:16-07:00","id":1407492,"title":"","content":"It might help to give another example from the persuade side of things. Let\u2019s say the same situation with Dave and Swan up above, except Dave has a major intimacy that \u201cpeople who never do things for themselves become weak and complacent\u201d. Okay so now swan has an in, if the people constantly come to Dave for help, they\u2019ll just be weakening themselves, so maybe this time he can sit it out, eh? Just to keep them standing on their own two feet.<br /> <br /> At that point Dave\u2019s player can\u2019t be like \u201cwell, I don\u2019t think Dave would buy that argument, a lot of innocent people might lose their lives or livelihood in those raids. They can remain strong in other ways like farming for themselves. I auto succeed against the influence.\u201d At that point Dave not buying the argument just means this influence isn\u2019t automatic, he gets his resolve. If his resolve gets beaten and he has no decision point to fall back on then in fact Dave DOES agree that if he goes and fights for them now that it will make the people weak and dependant. Dave has been convinced that making them fight for themselves is more important than stopping the raids, even if you the player don\u2019t agree with that assessment.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re bargaining with another character and what\u2019s on offer is valuable to the character in some way, even if it\u2019s a bad deal and not worth the offer, you\u2019re probably rolling bargain. Keeping in mind the sidebar on page 218 that not all role playing social scenes require the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T07:43:19-07:00","id":1407504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407457#post1407457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance's post is right here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1178525#post1178525\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...25#post1178525</a></div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s \u201cblatantly and obviously false\u201d and <i>then</i> there\u2019s the kinds of claims that question was about. Let\u2019s call those ones \u201cpatently ridiculous\u201d before you ask what the difference is as if it isn\u2019t obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 08-11-2020, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T07:57:22-07:00","id":1407505,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it the more I think that examples are the way to go, because otherwise \u201cget convinced to take a bad deal\u201d seems like it\u2019s just bullying or something.<br /> <br /> Say you\u2019re Frodo and Sam deep in Mordor, you\u2019re starving and exhausted, but you meet somebody who offers you food and rest if you let them gaze upon the ring for the duration of your stay. Probably a bad idea, but food when you\u2019re starving and rest when you\u2019re exhausted makes this valuable enough to roll on.<br /> <br /> Or you\u2019re Wonder Woman in the 2017 movie. Somebody offers you Ares in exchange for ceasing all interference with World War 1. Probably shouldn\u2019t take that deal, especially if your lover and new friends are major agents for the British who are not doing so hot. That\u2019s the whole reason you left your home though, to find Ares. That has enough value to roll, even if you shouldn\u2019t take the deal.<br /> <br /> Going back to LotR. You\u2019re an archer who\u2019s part of the fellowship leaving Rivendell and an elf asks you to take a package with you and deliver it to Edoras on your way by, but keep it to yourself. As payment an ancient bow crafted by the Noldor. It\u2019s shifty, you\u2019re being asked to keep secrets, but the payment is pretty sweet. If you\u2019re an ancient elf king with an entire armoury of such weapons just like what you\u2019re being offered back in your palace, then that\u2019s probably not special enough to be tempting. Otherwise, probably something you\u2019ll be applying resolve to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T12:05:25-07:00","id":1407563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407399#post1407399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave the Daring is a Dawn with the following intimacies:<br /> <br /> Defining &quot;I will get my sister's soul back from the Necromancer Galvan and put her to rest.&quot;<br /> Major Necromancer Galvan (Hatred)<br /> Major Kingdom of Swadia (Loyalty)<br /> Minor Cousin Dilliam (Disgust)<br /> <br /> Another character Swan the Suave is a legendary information broker, if you think you've got a secret, there's a 50% chance he already knows it, and a 100% chance that, given the opportunity, he's going to use it. Now, Swan hates Swadia. He thinks it sucks and wants it roughed up a little. Not destroyed, just, you know, a couple raiding parties here, a burned grainery there, that kind of thing. Sadly, Dave the Daring protects Swadia loyally.<br /> <br /> At this moment, he has no ability to convince Dave to sit this one out, a major request. There is no intimacy of Dave's that can be manipulated to get him to bench himself and not come to the aid of Swadia when it calls after him to fix their bandit problem. Persuade, as an action, is useless here. On the other hand, Swan knows the location of the Necromancer Galvan's hidden fortress, and what's more, he even knows that the soul of Dave's sister is being kept there. That information isn't free though. He wants it? He has to sit out this battle.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This example seems like a persuade action with some extra nuance. In essence, there's no difference: Swan appeals to Dave's defining intimacy to persuade him to do something, takes relevant penalties based on his credibility or lack thereof, and then rolls against Dave's resolve. If Dave fails, there's nothing he can do because none of his intimacies are powerful enough. To me, this seems no different to if he had attempted to persaude Dave rhetorically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407399#post1407399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we want to talk about bargaining for money or baubles or something, we're going to have to take a bit of a step back from epic heroes bargaining for the soul of the only person they've ever loved. I'm not saying that anyone should just be able to pull out some amount of silver and get to roll to get anything they want out of it. If somebody is offering your character a significant percentage of their current wealth to do something like take a detour, or deliver a package or something, that's worth rolling for.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting example, but I think it ultimately functions fine within the persuade system. If I make a rhetorical argument that you ought to do something, the force of my rhetoric alone is never going to be enough too convince you; I have to appeal to your thoughts, needs and/or desires (ie: your intimacies). Likewise, if I offer you money to do something, the amount of money alone won't convince you unless you have a reason to want that money.<br /> <br /> Now, most people are going to have reasons to want a shedload of money - they want to take care of their family, they want to escape the country to the city (or vice-versa), they want to keep their sick spouse healthy - but some might not. Immaculate monks (the righteous ones anyway) aren't likely to respond well to offers of material wealth, because they're not likely to have intimacies that could be appealed to by wealth. On the other hand, offering them a lost sacred text might have more appeal, but that would again be based on their intimacies of devotion to the Immaculate Faith and their desire for spiritual growth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407505#post1407505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say you\u2019re Frodo and Sam deep in Mordor, you\u2019re starving and exhausted, but you meet somebody who offers you food and rest if you let them gaze upon the ring for the duration of your stay. Probably a bad idea, but food when you\u2019re starving and rest when you\u2019re exhausted makes this valuable enough to roll on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I think I've broadly covered why I disagree with the other examples in the quoted post elsewhere in this post, this is a trickier one, since the offer appeals to needs lower on Maslow's hierarchy than the needs intimacies typically cover: Your fine feelings of herosim go by the wayside when the alternative is starvation. In this case I would say that the players and ST can agree that the need for food might become strong enough to represent an intimacy in its own right, in the same way an overpowering addiction might.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there might be intimacies that you could appeal to here through Sam or Frodo's stomach. Let's say Sam has a major tie of love for Rosie Cotton; he's not going to let himself die on this quest if it means he can't see Rosie again, so persuasion appealing to this intimacy with food seems valid. Likewise, most people are going to have something they want to keep on living for, and if they really don't... Well, people with no intimacies are either arhats or totally uninterested in the world, as implied by Cup Boils Over, so they'd have no reason to stick around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24811-grelkis","user":"Grelkis","date":".  More typos 08-11-2020, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24811-grelkis","name":"Grelkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24811_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T18:00:02-07:00","id":1407623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grelkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407563#post1407563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This example seems like a persuade action with some extra nuance. In essence, there's no difference: Swan appeals to Dave's defining intimacy to persuade him to do something, takes relevant penalties based on his credibility or lack thereof, and then rolls against Dave's resolve. If Dave fails, there's nothing he can do because none of his intimacies are powerful enough. To me, this seems no different to if he had attempted to persaude Dave rhetorically.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly similar, but it's also different. In a Persuade action the intimacy that you're leveraging must directly relate to the action being taken. As long as my bargainer, Swan, has this information about Galvan I can attempt to bargain almost anything from Dave. Doesn't really matter what it is, this info is super valuable to him so his ass is mine. Until I give it up, of course, which is the other thing that makes Bargain different from Persuade. If I could Persuade Dave not to respond to the call for his help, I lose nothing, but the info I can only give him once.<br /> <br /> Or I could lie, but in that case when the lie is revealed my reputation tanks, and good luck being an information broker with a reputation for lying.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to something else...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grelkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407563#post1407563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, most people are going to have reasons to want a shedload of money</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true, and not even just for reasons like wanting to stay fed. Maybe you've wanted your whole life to see the wondrous city of glass Chiaroscuro, well this money will not only fund a trip there, but one where you get to stay in luxury while you do it. The nice thing from my bargainer's perspective is, I don't have to know that. If I Persuade you, I <i>need </i>an intimacy to key off of, and a specific one. If I'm bargaining for something all I have to do is offer payment.<br /> <br /> Again though, the reason you can't just blindly do this all the time is because you give up something every time, and what you give up is usually proportional to the power of the person you're influencing. Wanna know how much jade it takes to bribe a Dynast into sneaking you into the Imperial Treasury? It might be cheaper to buy a few armies and storm the place.<br /> <br /> This applies to Threaten too, as well as Bargain. Pretty much everyone wants to live, if you threaten to kill them that'll get you some traction for almost anything you want to do. It will also probably instantly gain you a new enemy, so good luck using Threaten in every situation. There's also the chance they just successfully apply their resolve, and now you've got an enemy and didn't even gain anything from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grelkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402763-a-devil-s-bargain-roll?p=1407563#post1407563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maslow's hierarchy than the needs</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, intimacies do not cover things like this at all. Nobody has an intimacy for &quot;I want to be fed, with shelter, and security&quot;. That's why intimacies represent &quot;rerlationships, beliefs, ideals and goals&quot; and not basic needs or simple human nature. Like again nobody really has an intimacy for &quot;I really don't like to do pointless annoying tasks that take forever&quot;. Somebody could have an intimacy for that, but if they do it represents a very uncommon aversion to it. If somebody makes you till a field that isn't going to be planted one more time you will <i>literally </i>kill them, kind of thing.<br /> <br /> But, like, why? Why aren't basic needs and stuff intimacies? Shouldn't it be harder to persuade somebody to do something if it endangers one of those needs? Well, yes, that's why you have to meet a bare minimum of Minor/Major/Defining intimacy to persuade somebody to do something that inconveniences them, risks harming them, or risks death respectively. If you're threatening somebody's most basic needs for life, and you don't have a Defining intimacy to key off of, you auto-fail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some more examples of where bargain would be best used:<br /> <br /> A raiding party from a local dynasty-run kingdom has taken some of your friends as slaves, on orders from their matriarch. You bargain for them, offering 10 thoroughbred horses instead. He's going against the explicit orders of his matriarch, but surely 10 absolute unit horses is better than 10 unskilled and sickly slaves.<br /> <br /> You need access to the imperial treasury, and you happen to know someone who works there who's a bit low on cash at the moment. You fix his jade problem, and he leads you into one of the archives without saying a word about it.<br /> <br /> There's a small gaggle of street urchins in town, you know they wander the market picking pockets, and jingle a weighty little pouch of silver in front of them in exchange for any information about a woman with snow-white hair and a turtle-man bodyguard passing through the area. Might normally be an automatic thing, but this particular group was warned by their friends that anyone caught talking to people asking after that woman end up disappearing.<br /> <br /> Offering to make a sizable donation to the local struggling immaculate temple, one large enough to completely redo the exterior and make it something that inspires awe and wonder in all who live near it, but in return the monk has to point you towards a fugitive he's been hiding.<br /> <br /> Going to see a local emperor and offering them five different exotic animals, all incredibly rare, from the five corners of Creation. However, they must give up their prized Sunset Hummingbird, which is the last of its kind. Actually it's not, it an old Lunar friend of yours trapped in an artifact cage in the form of an extinct hummingbird, but the emperor doesn't need to know that.<br /> <br /> Safe access to the ancient first age tomb that a rebel faction in the south is using as a home base, and in return you give them enough firedust to fill their weapons for months more of hard fighting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}